# AQIS lab, Sprint 1 (WP-1.1), GPU stack for the NeMo models. The lock is s1-nemo.txt.
#
# Regenerate the lock from the repository root with uv 0.8.17 after editing this file or phase0.txt:
#   uv pip compile requirements/aqis_lab/s1-nemo.in -c requirements/aqis_lab/phase0.txt --python-version 3.13 --python-platform x86_64-manylinux_2_28 --generate-hashes --output-file requirements/aqis_lab/s1-nemo.txt
# Pass the same command as --custom-compile-command so the lock header records it, and update the line below to the
# SHA-256 of the phase0.txt it was compiled against.
# compiled-against: requirements/aqis_lab/phase0.txt sha256 87a1cc34c6d41388cf8ce1e415f95f61c3b24a7bc45b69a828a957c1813fdcef
#
# Own virtual environment on Colab. NeMo 3.0.0 as in the phase 0 GPU lock: Parakeet TDT v2 and Parakeet Unified (ASR) and
# Canary-Qwen (SpeechLM2, SALM.generate with audios and audio_lens).
# What the runner imports besides the stack: numpy, pyarrow, pyyaml (the config), soundfile (wav files for NeMo).
numpy
pyarrow
pyyaml
soundfile
huggingface_hub
nemo-toolkit[asr,speechlm2]==3.0.0
# torchao 0.15 and later import torch.nn.functional names (ScalingType, SwizzleType, scaled_grouped_mm) that torch 2.9.1, the
# version NeMo 3.0.0 pins, does not have, and transformers 5.x then imports torchao when it is 0.15 or newer, which
# broke `import nemo.collections.speechlm2.models` (Canary-Qwen) on the Colab smoke run of 19 Oct 2026. Below 0.15
# transformers leaves torchao alone (TORCHAO_MIN_VERSION) and 0.14.x is built for torch 2.9; nothing here quantizes.
torchao<0.15
